From e42bc071d422ddd65c7805d45b76319f8f28f117 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glib Shpychka <23005347+gshpychka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:54:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agents): accept answers from the requester's chat after
 delegated work finishes

When a subagent, a Claude Code session or a sessions_send follow-up finishes,
OpenClaw continues the requester's session in an internal turn. A question
that turn asks only accepts answers from a caller with the internal turn's
authority, so a reply from the chat that started the work is refused.

The turn that delegates the work records its caller facts on the run:
sessions_spawn for subagent, ACP and visible runs, and sessions_send for the
follow-up run it registers or its private follow-up request. A turn that
adopts a running child takes over its caller. The completion handoff carries
the caller that every finished run shares, and the completion turn checks
answers against that caller when its handoff exactly matches the turn,
including a source that keeps no subagent tool-policy envelope. A
sessions_send reply registers the same handoff, and a completion without
internal events names its child through its provenance. Replies from other
senders, turns without a matching handoff, and revoked settle batches are
still refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
